Subject: upstream: fix ownership and lifetime of several bits of state that persist for the life of the connection
Client-side connection state, including the cached host key, could be freed too early on some paths and then used after free. The fix moves ownership of those objects so they live for the whole connection. This backport keeps the upstream change but adapts it to the 10.2p1 call sites.

Origin: backport, https://github.com/openssh/openssh-portable/commit/e8bdfb151a356d0171fea4194dd205fbb252be23
CVE: CVE-2026-60002
Base-Tree: alpine 3.23-stable openssh 10.2_p1-r1
Adaptation: Rebased onto 10.2p1 after the DHI 0001-0008 patches. The static ssh_conn_info_free copy in ssh.c is dropped in favour of the sshconnect.c definition, ssh_login keeps the 10.2p1 call form with &hostaddr, and verify_host_key receives a sockaddr cast of the sockaddr_storage.
Verify: cmd `dhi def test package/apk/main/openssh/alpine-3.23/10.yaml` expect "ok"

